  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 215 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nShowers and a few storms may be ongoing across the area Thursday\nmorning but should push off to the southeast of the area during\nmorning hours. Highs are then expected to warm into the upper \n80s to the middle 90s Thursday afternoon, with heat index values\nin the upper 90s to around 100-105 degrees with the warmest \nreadings across the southwestern portions of the area.\n\nThe front will lift back to the north Thursday\nafternoon/evening. Instability will increase with the heating of\nthe day and some isolated storms will be possible across the\narea during the afternoon and early evening hours Thursday, but\ncoverage will be limited as lift will be more limited across \nthe area Thursday afternoon/early evening. \n\nAnother upper level disturbance will move southeast across the \nregion Thursday night into Friday and will push the front back \ninto the area. Scattered showers and storms will again be \npossible across portions of the area Thursday evening into \nFriday morning as the system moves through. Coverage may be more\nlimited especially further south so not all locations could be \nimpacted. Locally heavy rainfall will be possible again where \nthe the storms are able to develop and train over the same \nlocations. The activity should move off to the southeast Friday \nmorning, a few scattered showers and storms could linger across \nthe eastern portions of the area into Friday afternoon. \n\nAn upper level ridge will build over the plains this weekend\ninto early next week. Highs in the 90s with heat index values in\nthe upper 90s to 100-105 degrees each afternoon. The ensemble\nmodels are not indicating any widespread rain chances this\nweekend into early next week.",
